SUMMARY:Backpacking in Grayson Highlands State Park
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Adventures 30’s & 40’s\nJoin me for a 2.5-day ba
 ckpacking trip through the Grayson Highlands\, where we will get to experi
 ence incredible mountain views\, spectacular sunsets\, wildflowers\, majes
 tic forests\, and maybe even some wild ponies!\n\nThis backpacking trip wi
 ll begin *at the trailhead* at 10 am on Friday\, April 17th\, and we will 
 plan to finish before midday on Sunday.\n\nI have created a custom route w
 ith the link below.\n\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/cus
 tom-route-mount-rogers-loop-trail-53bd310?u=i&sh=p0nozs\n\nDay 1: We will 
 depart the trailhead at 10am\, hiking about 10 miles and just under 1\,700
  ft elevation.\nDay 2: We will begin our day early-to-mid morning\, and hi
 ke 12 miles and almost 2\,800 ft.\nDay 3: Sunday morning\, we will have ju
 st under 3 miles on mostly flat terrain to reach the trailhead\, with enou
 gh energy for the drive home!\n\nTotal distance for the 2.5 days will be j
 ust under 25 miles and 4\,500 ft vertical elevation gain. While this is no
 t specifically geared towards beginner backpackers\, I want all to feel we
 lcome. If I haven't hiked or backpacked with you before\, please feel free
  to still RSVP and I can reach out to you directly to review your experien
 ce and answer any questions!\n\nThere is a fee of $15 per vehicle to park 
 in the overnight backpacking lot. Please book your permit in advance using
  the link below!\nhttps://www.reservevaparks.com/Web/#!park/11\n\nBelow ar
 e a few housekeeping items that you must read in order to participate.\n\n
 1\\. You must come prepared with all of your own gear for overnight backpa
 cking\\\, including enough food for 2\\.5 days\\\, enough water \\(or the 
 ability to filter water\\)\\\, navigation\\\, and the ability to make it b
 ack to the trailhead on your own if separated\\\, etc\\.\n2\\. I am not a 
 certified guide\\\, nor will I be acting as the hiking guide for this trip
 \\. This is a social outing\\\, everyone will be responsible for their own
  navigation\\\, gear\\\, essentials\\\, etc\\. My goal is obviously to kee
 p everyone safe\\\, together\\\, and having a good time\\\, but I cannot g
 uarantee anyone's safety\\. By RSVPing "yes" to this event\\\, you are rel
 easing me from any\\-and\\-all liability should you experience illness\\\,
  injury\\\, or worse during \\(or as a result of\\) this trip\\.\n3\\. Thi
 s trail is dog\\-friendly and you are welcome to bring your dog IF you can
  guarantee that they will be kept on a leash AT ALL TIMES\\. Zero exceptio
 ns\\.\n4\\. Please brush up on your Leave No Trace Principles \\- https://
 www\\.nps\\.gov/articles/leave\\-no\\-trace\\-seven\\-principles\\.htm\n5\
 \. There are bears in the park\\\, so bring a bear canister\\. While there
  are some sites with bear boxes\\\, they are not guaranteed\\. It is also 
 not guaranteed that there will be trees to hang a bear bag\\\, so bear can
 isters are recommended\\.\n\nThis event has a short RSVP deadline because 
 of required permits. If you don't make an RSVP before the cutoff\, please 
 message me and I can check for availability of permits :-)\n\nThis will be
  an amazing trail\, can't wait to share it with all of you!
